":"2026-10-17T13:37:00-07:00","onset":"2026-10-17T13:37:00-07:00","expires":"2026-10-17T20:00:00-07:00","ends":"2026-10-17T20:00:00-07:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Moderate","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Heat Advisory","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA","headline":"Heat Advisory issued October 17 at 1:37PM PDT until October 17 at 8:00PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA","description":"* WHAT...Temperatures up to 95 expected.\n\n* WHERE...Los Angeles County Beaches, Los Angeles County Inland Coast\nincluding Downtown Los Angeles, Palos Verdes Hills, San Luis Obispo\nCounty Beaches, San Luis Obispo County Inland Central Coast, Santa\nBarbara County Central Coast Beaches, Santa Barbara County Inland\nCentral Coast, Santa Barbara County Southeastern Coast, and Santa\nBarbara County Southwestern Coast.\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM PDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hot temperatures may cause heat illnesses.","instruction":"Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.\n\nIn the event of a nearby wildfire, smoke may increase heat and\nphysical stress. If smoke impacts your area; 1) Have a cooling plan\nin place as smoke could limit your ability to cool your home through\nopen windows and 2) If you have air conditioning, set on air\nrecirculation within the home to avoid smoke exposure. Local\nofficials may have additional guidance.","response":"Execute","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["NPWLOX"],"WMOidentifier":["WWUS76 KLOX 172037"],"NWSheadline":["HEAT ADVISORY REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 8 PM PDT THIS EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KLOX.HT.Y.0019.000000T0000Z-261018T0300Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-10-17T20:00:00-07:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3fe9e5e2c0d2fbb2c976cc79fe9c3aab2f494327.003.1,2026-10-16T19:50:00-07